[%# The runner recipes.yaml, dumped whole by the recipe.

    YAML::XS::Dump rather than anything written here: Xslate has no dumper, and
    a recipes.yaml is an arbitrarily deep structure that a template has no
    business trying to indent correctly.

    Every store: reference in it was turned back into a secret: on the way
    through enrich, so what lands here names entries in the runner own keepass
    database and holds no passwords.  See SECRETS IN recipes in
    Provisioner::Recipe::trogrunner for why the indirection is spelled twice. -%]
[% recipes_yaml | mark_raw %]
